# promise: #663
# Arc's ⌘L on a page with the developer bar (a local page, GitHub #42) edits the bar's address in place: the panel
# covers the bar, the card's width with its top on the bar's, and the suggestions drop across the page (Arc 1.174.1,
# 22 Nov 2026). Scenarios start with Developer Mode off for the fixture server, so ⌘L first opens the centred bar, as
# Arc's does on an ordinary site; with Developer Mode on, the panel over the developer bar.
budget rss=600 stalls50=6
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=local
wait 3
cra://debug?key=l,37,1048576
wait 1
cra://debug?urlFieldEdit=state
expect-log url field state: not editing, command bar open, panel centred w=
cra://dismiss
wait 1
cra://action/toggleDeveloperMode
wait 1
cra://debug?key=l,37,1048576
wait 1
cra://debug?urlFieldEdit=state
expect-log url field state: not editing, command bar open, panel developer w=[0-9]+ h=[0-9]+ at bar
cra://dismiss
